        "title": "Carbon Nanostructures: Fullerenes, Nanotubes, Graphene",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Carbon forms multiple nanoscale allotropes with radically different properties.\nAll are built from sp2-hybridized carbon (graphene-like bonding) but differ in\ntopology: flat, cylindrical, spherical. The electronics, mechanics, and chemistry\nderive from the same benzene-ring C-C bonding network in different geometries."
